1 NAME Constança Antónia /Avellino/Avelino/
2 GIVN Constança Antónia
2 _MARNM Avellino/Avelino
1 NAME Dna. Constança Antónia Avellino/Avelino
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1757
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Reino de Portugal
1 OCCU Nobre
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Although his patrilineal surname was originally spelled Avellino, his grandfather's marriage to a Spanish woman and their move to the latter's country brought about a transformation in the family's paradigms.Such m
2 CONC etamorphoses were accentuated with his father's affective connection with the Kingdom of Portugal, culminating in the adaptation of the surname to the Iberian spelling. These however would not be the last or most significant metam
2 CONC orphoses experienced by the Avelino, which would be profoundly affected by the Napoleonic wars and by their connection to D. João VI's policy related to his main colony, more precisely, in the territory to the north of it, where, 
2 CONC , his son Jose Joaquim would settle down and with him, a new branch would start!
